---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Btn from '../components/Btn.astro';
import { AUTHOR, SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Contact" description="How to reach the publisher of this site for corrections, questions, permissions and press, and what to expect back.">
<div class="wrap"><Breadcrumbs trail={[{ label: 'Contact', href: '/contact/' }]} /></div>
<section class="wrap" style="padding:1.5rem 1.25rem 0">
  <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
  <h1 style="max-width:20ch">Contact</h1>
  <p style="max-width:46ch;font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:1.2rem 0 1.8rem">
    One address, read by a person. There is no ticket system, no contact form that goes nowhere, and no
    autoresponder.
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p style="font-size:1.15rem">
      <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Every message is read by {AUTHOR.name}, who writes and edits this site. Replies normally go out
      within two working days.
    </p>

    <h2>What to send, and what happens to it</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>If you are writing about</th><th>Include</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>A wrong figure</td>
          <td>The page, the figure, what you believe is correct, and the source</td>
          <td>Corrected in place with a dated note and logged publicly on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>, normally within 48 hours</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A fee or policy change we have missed</td>
          <td>The platform announcement or regulation, with a link</td>
          <td>Added to the <a href="/policy-log/">fee and policy log</a> with its date, and any affected guide is revisited</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>An operational question</td>
          <td>Enough context to answer usefully</td>
          <td>Answered where we can. Where the answer is genuinely useful to other sellers, it may become a guide — you will be asked first</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Permission to republish</td>
          <td>What you want to use and where</td>
          <td>Short quotes with attribution and a link need no permission. Anything more, ask</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Press or a speaking request</td>
          <td>Outlet, topic, deadline</td>
          <td>Answered directly</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Vendors and agencies</h2>
    <p>
      We do not accept sponsored posts, paid placement, link insertions, guest posts, or pre-publication
      review of anything. Offers of free product access are declined; when software reviews begin, tools
      will be bought at list price on the plan being reviewed. These are not negotiating positions and a
      follow-up email will not change them.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is welcome: a correction to something we have published about your product, with the
      documentation behind it. That gets the same treatment as any other correction.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account suspensions, appeals and plan-of-action letters. That needs someone with sight of your account.</li>
      <li>Tax, legal, customs classification and accounting questions. Nothing here is professional advice, and a 10-digit tariff code is not something to take from a website.</li>
      <li>Anything requiring access to your seller account or your data. We will not ask for credentials and you should not send them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is published by <strong>{SITE.publisher}</strong>, an independent business with no
      ownership relationship to any marketplace or software vendor covered here. Editorial responsibility
      sits with <a href="/about/">{AUTHOR.name}</a>. Funding, independence and disclosure rules are set out
      on the <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards page</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <Btn href="/corrections/">Report a correction</Btn>
      <Btn href="/about/" quiet={true}>Who writes this</Btn>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
